  "name": "Manufacture of fabricated metal products, except machinery and equipment",
  "section": "C",
  "summary": "Metal fabricators report AI in vision inspection, robotic welding, CNC programming, quoting and predictive maintenance, usually framed as a response to skilled-labour shortages. Many sell into the AI build-out: server racks and enclosures, cooling parts, prefabricated modules, utility structures, boilers and nuclear components for new power generation, precision parts for chip-making tools. Weapons and ammunition makers write about autonomy, AI-assisted targeting, loitering munitions and counter-drone systems, with human-control and regulatory questions attached.",
